---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navigation from "../components/Navigation.astro";
---

<Layout title="Our Story & Legacy | Ben's Christmas Tree Farm">
    <Navigation />

    <div class="background-overlay">
        <img src="/DJI_0850sm.jpg" alt="Ben's Christmas Tree Farm landscape" class="bg-image" />
    </div>

    <main class="content-container">
        <div class="glass-box legacy-dashboard">
            
            <header class="about-header">
                <h1>The Story Behind the Farm</h1>
                <p class="subtitle">Cultivating family memories for over 40 years</p>
            </header>

            <!-- SECTION 1: Text Left, Image Right on Desktop / Image First on Mobile -->
            <section class="story-row">
                <div class="text-block">
                    <h2>From the City to the Open Fields</h2>
                    <p>
                        Ben was born and raised in Chicago. But the seed for his true 
                        passion was planted hundreds of miles away as a boy, while he spent summers on his grandmother’s 
                        farm in Nebraska. It was there that he developed a deep, lifelong appreciation for the land and the simple 
                        peace of wide-open country air. 
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Years later, after earning his MBA, Ben found himself climbing the ladder in a cushy office job in downtown 
                        Chicago. The corporate life provided security, but his heart kept wandering back to those childhood summers. 
                        In search of that fresh country air, he made a leap of faith and in 1982 purchased 55 acres of rolling farmland in 
                        Harvard, Illinois - initially intending to plant and sell Christmas trees purely as a weekend hobby.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="image-block frame-cozy rotate-right">
                    <img src="/ben_horse.jpg" alt="A young Ben in Nebraska" />
                    <p class="caption">A young Ben in Nebraska</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- SECTION 2: Image Left, Text Right on Desktop / Image First on Mobile -->
            <section class="story-row reverse">
                <div class="image-block frame-cozy rotate-left">
                    <img src="/ben_cbk.jpg" alt="Ben with son and grandkids" />
                    <p class="caption">Three generations of Christmas Tree farmers</p>
                </div>
                <div class="text-block">
                    <h2>Growing the Green Way Before It Was Cool</h2>
                    <p>
                        Ben quickly realized that a thriving tree farm demanded far more attention than a casual weekend 
                        hobby would allow. Turning his dreams into reality, Ben left his office job behind, permanently 
                        trading a suit and tie for a tractor and dirt. 
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Long before "organic" and "eco-friendly" became buzzwords, Ben was fiercely dedicated to growing 
                        trees the green way. He refused to expose himself, his children, or his customers to chemicals, instead
                        pioneering a strict 100% herbicide-free and pesticide-free approach which continues at the farm today.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <!-- SECTION 3: Text Left, Image Right on Desktop / Image First on Mobile -->
            <section class="story-row">
                <div class="text-block">
                    <h2>Carrying the Torch Forward</h2>
                    <p>
                        Though Ben passed away in 2013, his dream and his legacy live on. Today, his sons Chris and Justin have 
                        proudly taken over management of the farm, alongside a longtime family friend who is pouring his blood, 
                        sweat, and tears into the farm every single day. 
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Between 2017 and 2018, the farm was expanded to 100 acres to meet the demand for high quality, naturally-grown Christmas trees.
                        The legacy that Ben left lives on vibrantly through his sons, the thousands of local families who 
                        make our fields part of their annual traditions, and his ten beloved grandchildren who will grow up with the 
                        farm in their blood. We invite you to come out and be a part of the Ben's family!
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="image-block frame-cozy rotate-right">
                    <img src="/ben_cj.jpg" alt="Ben with sons Chris and Justin" />
                    <p class="caption">Ben with sons Chris and Justin</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <hr class="divider" />

            <!-- BOTTOM DECK: The Album Collage Grid -->
            <section class="scrapbook-section">
                <h3>Memories Scattered Through the Rows</h3>
                <p class="scrapbook-intro">A glimpse into life on the farm across generations, from grandfathers to grandkids.</p>
                
                <div class="scrapbook-grid">
                    <div class="scrapbook-item frame-cozy item-1">
                        <img src="/ben_and_ben.jpg" alt="Ben smiling with his grandson" />
                        <span class="scrapbook-caption">Ben with grandson Ben</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="scrapbook-item frame-cozy item-2">
                        <img src="/ben_and_kbaby.jpg" alt="Ben with baby granddaughter" />
                        <span class="scrapbook-caption">Ben with his granddaughter</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="scrapbook-item frame-cozy item-3">
                        <img src="/ben_sis.jpg" alt="Ben with his sister" />
                        <span class="scrapbook-caption">Ben with his sister</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="scrapbook-item frame-cozy item-4">
                        <img src="/ben_and_k.jpg" alt="Ben with his granddaughter" />
                        <span class="scrapbook-caption">Ben with his granddaughter</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </section>

        </div>
    </main>
</Layout>

<style>
    /* UTILITY CONTAINER CONTROLS */
    .background-overlay {
        position: fixed;
        top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; z-index: -1;
        background-color: #0d1a0d;
    }
    .bg-image { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; opacity: 0.15; }

    .content-container {
        display: flex; justify-content: center;
        padding: 120px 20px 60px;
    }

    .legacy-dashboard {
        max-width: 950px; width: 100%;
        background: rgba(20, 32, 20, 0.9);
        backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
        border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
        padding: 3rem; border-radius: 12px; color: #f4efe6;
    }

    .about-header { border-bottom: 2px solid #109661; padding-bottom: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 3rem; text-align: center; }
    .about-header h1 { font-family: Georgia, serif; font-size: 2.5rem; margin: 0; color: #ffffff; }
    .subtitle { font-style: italic; color: #a3cea0; font-size: 1.1rem; margin-top: 0.5rem; }

    /* MOBILE EDITORIAL SYSTEM (FALLBACK ENGINE) */
    .story-row {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column; /* Stacks linearly on mobile screens */
        gap: 2rem; 
        margin-bottom: 4rem;
    }

    /* THE MAGIC REORDER HOOK FOR SMARTPHONES */
    .story-row .image-block {
        order: 1; /* Forces picture to render first at the top of the stack */
        width: 100%;
        max-width: 320px;
        margin: 0 auto;
    }
    .story-row .text-block {
        order: 2; /* Drops the narrative blocks below the picture node */
    }

    .text-block h2 { font-family: Georgia, serif; font-size: 1.75rem; margin-top: 0; color: #ffffff; }
    .text-block p { line-height: 1.7; font-size: 1.05rem; opacity: 0.95; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }

    /* THE HOMEY / COZY SCRAPBOOK PHOTO FRAME */
    .frame-cozy {
        background: #ffffff; padding: 0.75rem 0.75rem 2rem;
        box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5), 0 2px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2);
        border-radius: 2px; transition: transform 0.3s ease-in-out;
        box-sizing: border-box;
    }
    .frame-cozy img { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 1px; }
    .frame-cozy .caption, .frame-cozy .scrapbook-caption {
        font-family: "Permanent Marker", "Courier New", cursive, serif;
        color: #2b3e2b; text-align: center; font-size: 0.95rem; margin: 0.75rem 0 0; font-weight: bold;
    }

    /* Rotations stay clean across both viewports */
    .rotate-right { transform: rotate(1.5deg); }
    .rotate-left { transform: rotate(-1.5deg); }
    .frame-cozy:hover { transform: rotate(0deg) scale(1.02); }

    .divider { border: 0; height: 1px; background: linear-gradient(to right, transparent, rgba(255,255,255,0.15), transparent); margin: 4rem 0; }

    /* ALBUM SCRAPBOOK GRID (BOTTOM DECK) */
    .scrapbook-section { text-align: center; }
    .scrapbook-section h3 { font-family: Georgia, serif; font-size: 1.6rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
    .scrapbook-intro { font-size: 1rem; opacity: 0.8; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; font-style: italic; }

    .scrapbook-grid {
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        justify-content: center;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 2.5rem;
        margin-top: 2rem;
    }

    .scrapbook-item.frame-cozy {
        background: #ffffff;
        width: 220px; 
        padding: 0.75rem 0.75rem 2.25rem;
        box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4), 0 2px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15);
        border-radius: 2px;
        box-sizing: border-box;
        transition: transform 0.3s ease-in-out, z-index 0s;
    }

    .scrapbook-item.frame-cozy img {
        width: 100%;
        height: 200px;
        object-fit: cover;
        display: block;
        border: 1px solid #f0f0f0;
    }

    .scrapbook-caption {
        font-family: "Permanent Marker", "Courier New", cursive, serif;
        color: #2b3e2b;
        text-align: center;
        font-size: 0.9rem;
        font-weight: bold;
        display: block;
        margin-top: 0.75rem;
        line-height: 1.2;
        white-space: normal;
    }

    .item-1 { transform: rotate(-3deg); }
    .item-2 { transform: rotate(2.5deg); }
    .item-3 { transform: rotate(-2deg); }
    .item-4 { transform: rotate(4deg); }

    .scrapbook-item.frame-cozy:hover {
        transform: rotate(0deg) scale(1.06);
        z-index: 10;
        box-shadow: 0 15px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);
    }

    /* DESKTOP MATRIX ACTUATOR: Shifts to rigid side-by-side grids on monitors */
    @media (min-width: 768px) {
        .story-row { 
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 0.8fr; 
            gap: 3.5rem; 
            align-items: center;
        }
        
        .story-row.reverse { 
            grid-template-columns: 0.8fr 1.2fr; 
        }

        /* Desktop resets: lets the DOM positions naturally govern left/right placement */
        .story-row .image-block { order: unset; }
        .story-row .text-block { order: unset; }

        .image-block.frame-cozy {
            width: 100%;
            max-width: 340px;
            margin: 0 auto;
        }

        .image-block.frame-cozy img {
            width: 100%;
            height: auto;
            max-height: 400px;
            object-fit: cover;
            display: block;
        }
        
        .scrapbook-grid { 
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); 
        }
    }
</style>